/-!
# Substrate for Tag 0E7H, clauses (2) and (4): the globally generated case

[Stacks, Tag 0E7H] fixes a proper morphism `f : X ⟶ Y` with `dim(X_y) ≤ 1` and
`H¹(X_y, 𝒪_{X_y}) = 0` for every `y ∈ Y`, and a quasi-coherent `ℱ` on `X`, and asserts

1. `Rᵖ f_* ℱ = 0` for `p > 1`,
2. `R¹ f_* ℱ = 0` if there is a surjection `f^*𝒢 ⟶ ℱ` with `𝒢` quasi-coherent on `Y`,

and, when `Y` is affine,

3. `Hᵖ(X, ℱ) = 0` for `p ∉ {0, 1}`,
4. `H¹(X, ℱ) = 0` if `ℱ` is globally generated.

All four clauses are proved in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/TopDegreeBaseChange/FibreDimensionOneCohomologyVanishing.lean`;
clauses (2) and (4) there are `isZero_higherDirectImage_one_of_epi_pullback_of_isProper` and
`isZero_cohomology_one_of_generatingSections_of_isAffine`. This file holds substrate for those
two clauses: the passage of global generation from the base to the preimage of an affine open,
and a route to `R¹ f_* 𝒪_X = 0` through [Stacks, Tag 0E7G].

## The source's argument, and what it needs

The source proves (4) first. If `ℱ` is globally generated there is a surjection
`⨁_{i ∈ I} 𝒪_X ⟶ ℱ`; by clause (1) and the long exact sequence of cohomology the induced map on
`H¹` is surjective, so it suffices that `H¹(X, ⨁_{i ∈ I} 𝒪_X) = 0`, which follows from
`H¹(X, 𝒪_X) = 0` because `H¹(X, -)` commutes with direct sums ([Stacks, Tag 01FF]). That whole
paragraph is already carried out in `OneDimensionalFibres.lean`, granted `H¹(X, 𝒪_X) = 0` as a
hypothesis.

The vanishing of `H¹(X, 𝒪_X)` is **not** an instance of clause (4) applied to `𝒪_X` — that
would be circular, `𝒪_X` being globally generated by its unit section. The source gets it from
[Stacks, Tag 0E7G], a different tag: the fibrewise hypothesis `H¹(X_y, 𝒪_{X_y}) = 0` makes
`R¹ f_* 𝒪_X` vanish on a neighbourhood of each `y`, hence everywhere, hence
`H¹(X, 𝒪_X) = H⁰(Y, R¹ f_* 𝒪_X) = 0` over an affine base. [Stacks, Tag 0E7G] is available in
this development as
`exists_isOpen_isZero_restrict_firstDirectImage_of_isZero_cohomologyOne_fiber`,
granted its own two hypotheses `hft` and `hbc`; that route is the one taken here, in
`isZero_firstDirectImageStructureSheaf`.

Clause (2) is then local on `Y`: over an affine open `V ⊆ Y` the module `𝒢|_V` is globally
generated, hence so is its pullback along `f ∣_ V`, hence so is `ℱ|_{f⁻¹(V)}`
(`generatingSectionsRestrictPreimage`); clause (4) kills `H¹(f⁻¹(V), ℱ|_{f⁻¹(V)})`, which over
the affine `V` is the vanishing of `R¹ (f ∣_ V)_* (ℱ|_{f⁻¹(V)})` ([Stacks, Tags 01XJ] and
[01XK]), and that is the restriction of `R¹ f_* ℱ` to `V` by [Stacks, Tag 01E5]. Vanishing on an
affine open cover of `Y` is vanishing.

## Main results

All in the namespace `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TopDegreeBaseChange`.

* `isZero_firstDirectImageStructureSheaf`: `R¹ f_* 𝒪_X = 0`, from the fibrewise hypothesis
  through [Stacks, Tag 0E7G]. This is the step that replaces the circular appeal to clause (4)
  at `𝒪_X`.
* `FirstDirectImageFiniteTypeOfFibreDimensionOne` and
  `FirstDirectImageCommutesBaseChangeOfFibreDimensionOne`: the two hypotheses of
  [Stacks, Tag 0E7G] in this development, quantified over all proper morphisms with fibres of
  dimension at most one.
* `pullbackRestrictComparison` and `generatingSectionsRestrictPreimage`: untagged substrate, the
  commutation of pullback with restriction to an open of the target and its consequence that
  `ℱ|_{f⁻¹(V)}` is globally generated.

## Two carried hypotheses, neither of them a case of this tag

* `hft` is the **finite-type** clause of [Stacks, Tag 0EX4] at degree one for the structure
  sheaf, quantified over all proper morphisms with fibres of dimension at most one. Only the
  *quasi-coherence* clause of that tag is formalized in this development
  (`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProperQcoh/Basic.lean` and
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/HigherDirectImageQcqs/Qcqs.lean`); the finite-type clause is
  nowhere available unconditionally for `d ≥ 1`, see
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/TopDegreeFiniteType/`.
* `hbc` is the base-change clause [Stacks, Tag 0EX3] (b) for the structure sheaf in degree one,
  in the shape `FirstDirectImageCommutesBaseChange` that `ContractingRationalCurves.lean`
  already uses, again quantified over all proper morphisms with fibres of dimension at most one.
  Of [Stacks, Tag 0EX3] only (a) is formalized, in `BaseChangeVanishing.lean`.

Neither is a vanishing statement in degree one about a quasi-coherent module, which is what
clauses (2) and (4) assert, and neither mentions `f` or `ℱ`.

## Implementation notes

Cohomology is `Hⁱ(X, ℱ) = ((moduleGlobalSections X).rightDerivedPlus i).obj ℱ` and higher direct
images are `((Scheme.Modules.pushforward p).rightDerivedPlus i).obj ℱ`, as throughout this
directory; `H¹(X_y, 𝒪_{X_y})` is `firstCohomologyStructureSheaf (f.fiber y)` and `R¹ f_* 𝒪_X` is
`firstDirectImageStructureSheaf f`, the abbreviations of `ContractingRationalCurves.lean`.

"Globally generated" is Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections`, as in
`OneDimensionalFibres.lean`.

`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules X` is a `def` for `SheafOfModules X.ringCatSheaf` with its own
`Category` instance, so an `Epi` or a `PreservesColimitsOfSize` fact proved in one spelling is
not found by instance search in the other. Every such fact is therefore passed as an explicit
argument — which is what `AlgebraicGeometry.generatingSectionsOfEpi` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.generatingSectionsMap` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/QuasiCoherent/FinitePresentationExtension.lean` exist for — and
`hpres` is bound by a `have` so that its statement is elaborated in the `Scheme.Modules`
spelling before it crosses.

